# moonshine
## Containers, containers, containers

| image | what's in it | size |
|---|---|---|
| `moonshine-base:brush` | musl + brush as `/bin/sh`, no busybox | 7.92 MB |
| `moonshine-brush:latest` | brush alone, on `FROM scratch`, no libc at all | 6.06 MB |
| `moonshine-apk:latest` | the same, plus apk, so it can install packages | 14.4 MB |
| `moonshine-sway:latest` | sway on top of the apk image, no mesa at all | 82.1 MB |

brush is the only shell. There is no busybox, no ash, and by default no
coreutils either

## What is in which package
Which of the usual tools each userland actually ships. The Alpine 3.24 columns
are counted from the packages themselves (`apk info -L`); u-root and gokrazy
from their own repositories. Not from memory -- both coreutils are split into
subpackages on Alpine, so the obvious answer is wrong in a few places.

| | tools |
|---|--:|
| GNU `coreutils` | 102 |
| `uutils-coreutils` | 107 |
| moonshine `uutils` | 22 |
| `util-linux` | 124 |
| `procps-ng` | 17 |
| `busybox` | 304 |
| `u-root` | 117 |
| `gokrazy` | 0 |

